.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH apmw 1  "apmw 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
apmw \- All Package Manager Wrapper
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBapmw\fR [\fB\-\-install\fR] [\fB\-\-uninstall\fR] [\fB\-\-intercept\fR] [\fB\-\-shell\fR] [\fB\-\-man\fR] [\fB\-\-usage\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-human\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-debug\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-\-interactive\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-scan\fR] [\fB\-\-scan\-only\fR] [\fB\-\-on\-risk\fR] [\fB\-\-update\-security\-db\fR] [\fB\-\-fields\fR] [\fB\-\-full\fR] [\fB\-\-daemon\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-daemon\fR] [\fB\-\-list\-jobs\fR] [\fB\-\-cancel\-job\fR] [\fB\-\-manager\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-telemetry\fR] [\fB\-\-telemetry\-preview\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Abstracts every package installer into one intelligent surface.
Detects the correct package manager, installs tools with install\-on\-use
semantics, and runs security scanning before install.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-install\fR
Generate shell completions and initialize the config file
.TP
\fB\-\-uninstall\fR
Remove generated completions and config (best\-effort cleanup)
.TP
\fB\-\-intercept\fR
Install or remove PATH shims that intercept package manager calls (used with `\-\-install` or `\-\-uninstall`)
.TP
\fB\-\-shell\fR \fI<SHELL>\fR
Shell to generate completions for (used with \-\-install)
.TP
\fB\-\-man\fR
Print the man page to stdout (groff/troff format) and exit.

The output can be piped to `man \-l \-` or saved to a file under `man/man1/apmw.1`. Equivalent to `man apmw` once installed.
.TP
\fB\-\-usage\fR
Print a brief usage summary and exit.

Shows a one\-line synopsis and the most common commands, suitable for quick reference. Use `\-\-help` for the full description.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit output as JSON (machine\-readable)
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR [default: auto]
Color output: auto, always, never
.TP
\fB\-\-human\fR
Human\-readable output (escape hatch for AXI/TOON mode)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Increase verbosity (can be repeated: \-v, \-vv)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress non\-error output
.TP
\fB\-\-debug\fR
Enable debug\-level diagnostics
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would happen without making changes
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Force the operation, bypassing confirmations
.TP
\fB\-\-interactive\fR
Enable interactive/TUI mode
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR
Disable pager output
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-scan\fR
Skip security scanning
.TP
\fB\-\-scan\-only\fR
Only run the security scan, then exit
.TP
\fB\-\-on\-risk\fR \fI<ACTION>\fR
Action to take when a security scan detects risk
.TP
\fB\-\-update\-security\-db\fR
Update the security vulnerability database before scanning
.TP
\fB\-\-fields\fR \fI<LIST>\fR
Comma\-separated list of fields to include in AXI minimal output
.TP
\fB\-\-full\fR
Show full content (escape hatch for AXI truncation)
.TP
\fB\-\-daemon\fR
Run in daemon mode (long\-running background process)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-daemon\fR
Disable daemon mode (force synchronous operation)
.TP
\fB\-\-list\-jobs\fR
List background jobs
.TP
\fB\-\-cancel\-job\fR \fI<ID>\fR
Cancel a background job by ID
.TP
\fB\-\-manager\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Override auto\-detection and force a specific package manager.

When set, detection is skipped entirely and the specified manager is used. Valid values cover all supported package managers across ecosystems. See `\-\-help` for the full list.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-telemetry\fR
Disable telemetry collection for this invocation
.TP
\fB\-\-telemetry\-preview\fR
Print the telemetry payload that would be sent without actually sending it
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
apmw\-install(1)
Install a package or tool
.TP
apmw\-detect(1)
Detect the package manager for the current project
.TP
apmw\-status(1)
Show apmw status and audit log
.TP
apmw\-clone(1)
Create a historyless clone of a repository with AST indexing
.TP
apmw\-scan(1)
Scan a package (or the current project) for security issues
.TP
apmw\-suggest(1)
Suggest within\-ecosystem alternatives for a package
.TP
apmw\-info(1)
Show detailed info about a package
.TP
apmw\-audit\-log(1)
Show the audit log of past operations
.TP
apmw\-config(1)
View or initialize apmw configuration
.TP
apmw\-governance(1)
Manage governance rules (refresh the spec, show current rules)
.TP
apmw\-intercept(1)
Intercept a package manager call (invoked by PATH shims)
.TP
apmw\-mcp(1)
Start the MCP (Model Context Protocol) server over stdio
.TP
apmw\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0

